## Numan tests its health-coaching agent through the same graph it ships

Source: LangChain — https://www.langchain.com/blog/how-numan-built-an-eval-first-ai-health-coach-with-langgraph-and-langsmith
Published: 2026-10-19
Channel: news

Numan describes an evaluation architecture for Nu, its health-coaching agent, that avoids maintaining a separate imitation of production. Tests exercise the same LangGraph graph used by the application, including its supervisor, specialist agents, and safety guards. LangSmith records real and simulated conversations as traces and holds the datasets, experiments, and reviewer annotations. This keeps the measured system aligned with the deployed implementation rather than a copied prompt.

The team replaced a single average score with category-level judgments and narrowed single-turn rubrics to behavior one reply can actually demonstrate. Existing safety probes gate releases, while daily human review checks sampled conversations. A newer simulated-conversation layer lets a model play a responsive persona instead of following a fixed script. That layer remains a prototype: its engineering-written criteria do not gate releases or support safety claims until clinician sign-off. Continuous online evaluation is also described as a next step, not an operating capability. The case study offers implementation lessons, not independently verified clinical outcomes.

Why it matters: Keep evaluation on the production execution path and distinguish validated gates from experimental checks.

