## Braintrust’s SDK expands trace capture and preserves records when customizers fail

Source: Braintrust — https://github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-javascript/releases/tag/braintrust%403.38.0
Published: 2026-10-19
Channel: github

Braintrust’s JavaScript SDK 3.38.0 expands the calls and payloads captured by its instrumentation while tightening several failure paths. The stable October 19 release lists image-input capture for its typesafe integration, decision-call and media tracing for the AI SDK integration, and Decisions API tracing for the OpenAI integration. It also adds OpenTelemetry span-customizer support; the companion @braintrust/otel 1.1.0 release carries that same feature and updated SDK dependency.

The more consequential reliability detail is a native-SDK fix for customizer failures. The linked pull request says exceptions or invalid hook returns stop processing and export a stripped record rather than dropping it. Identity, routing fields and existing duration timestamps survive, while content and prior hook mutations are removed and the context indicates a customizer error. Failed-record attachment uploads are suppressed.

That behavior preserves evidence that a span existed without exporting the payload a failed hook might have been intended to protect. It is not retroactive redaction: the pull request explicitly says earlier successful exports cannot be retracted, and the fix’s scope is native spans rather than a blanket change to OpenTelemetry behavior. Operators should test those boundaries with their actual customization and export paths.

Why it matters: Test both successful customization and throwing hooks: retaining a minimal failure record is different from retaining its potentially sensitive payload.

