## Elastic details the typed foundation for declarative OpenTelemetry .NET configuration

Source: Elastic Observability Labs — https://www.elastic.co/observability-labs/blog/opentelemetry-dotnet-declarative-configuration
Published: 2026-10-19
Channel: news

Elastic explains early work toward declarative configuration in the OpenTelemetry .NET SDK. A new package parses YAML into a typed model before projecting supported values into the IConfiguration interface the SDK already consumes. The intermediate model preserves distinctions between missing, null, and present values that would disappear if the parser immediately flattened everything into strings. This is a foundation for operating telemetry configuration separately from application instrumentation code.

The initial implementation is intentionally narrow: it covers file format, disabling the SDK, resource attributes, and environment-variable substitution. The broader plan still includes component creation and other configuration capabilities. Dynamic reload is explicitly outside these first steps; configuration changes apply at application launch rather than silently updating running providers. Elastic says a public alpha will follow the core phases, with design details still open to change. For teams instrumenting AI services in .NET, the relevance is a prospective standardized control surface for telemetry, not a newly available production-ready sampler-management feature.

Why it matters: Track the upstream implementation, but do not mistake its configuration foundation for complete or reloadable SDK control.

